Z||000001||Black88GT||11-20-2000||04:13 PM||||Good luck.  I have been looking and emailing for a couple months, no one wants to sell just the block.  I assume you want to do the 3.4 swap?  Thats why I want just the block too.  LMK if you find anyone<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||11-20-2000||05:09 PM||||fiero56,<P>I might have a lead on some up in MI.  Are you going to be using one of your existing blocks as a core? <P>You still haven't called me... I will be at work until around 7 p.m. tonight (513.576.6200 x 215) <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000003||fiero56||11-20-2000||06:53 PM||||William, I could use one as a core. Would prefer to give up the '86 block rather than the '88. Supposedly '88 block has better oiling system, along with a few other improvements. I would prefer not to pay more than $100 for a block, since I can get a complete L/B for $400.<P>I'll try to call you now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-20-2000||10:15 PM||||Black88GT:<P>That is exactly what I'm looking for. I have been sending e-mails, running searches, and placed a few calls. I haven't found just blocks. I have everything I would need short of a 3.1 crank, and 3.4 block. I'm running out of options. WTIII gave me a few local yards to check. My few experiences with yards though, is that they ask way too much for a v-6($1000+), unrebuilt. That's nuts. <A HREF="http://www.tacreations.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreations.com</A>  has 3.4 longblocks starting at $350. But I just want a block, and don't want to spend that much. I have 3 engines and two cars as it is. I'll make a few more calls tommorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-21-2000||09:35 PM||||Made a half dozen or so more calls today. Didn't find any blocks, cheapest I found was out of a '94 Camaro, 50,000 miles, unrebuilt, $650+core. Don't know what core was.<P>I did find a place that will re-grind my crank, balance, magna-flux, and regrind the oil holes, all for $75. Beats the $85 just for the grind I was quoted elsewhere. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
